3. Interoperability — the product should conform, not invent

A patient summary is already a defined, standardised artefact internationally. Conforming to it lowers integration risk and strengthens the “source-attributed” claim.

Standard

What it defines

Relevance

Grade

HL7 International Patient Summary (IPS); ISO 27269:2021; FHIR IG STU1

A minimal, non-exhaustive, condition-independent summary. Required sections: Allergies/Intolerances, Medication Summary, Problem List. Recommended: Immunizations, Results, Procedures, Medical Devices. Optional: Vital Signs, Past Illness, Social History, Plan of Care, etc.

Directly maps to the MVP sections. Adopt IPS section model so “history + reports” is standards-based and portable.

[V-P]

ABDM FHIR profiles / HI types (DiagnosticReport, Prescription, OPConsultation, DischargeSummary, WellnessRecord, etc.)

The record bundle types ABDM exchanges via consent.

Defines what “external records” (phase 2, MR-6) can contain and how appointments/reports surface.

