6. Evidence summary & confidence

• STRONG (verified): the general clinician EHR/chart-review time burden; the India regulatory regime (DPDP, ABDM HDM, HIP/HIU); interoperability standards (IPS, FHIR, EHR Standards for India); national digitisation scale.

• MODERATE (reasoned): competitive gaps inferred from official documentation; segment prioritisation logic.

• WEAK / ABSENT (requires primary work): India OPD-specific magnitude of the problem; demand for a separate dashboard vs. improving the HMIS; willingness to pay; buyer economics; segment counts for sizing.

Bottom line: the problem class and the compliance/interoperability terrain are well-evidenced and ready to design against. The market case for THIS product is a credible, well-structured hypothesis — not yet a proven market. The 8-week validation gate (MRD §6) is the mechanism that converts hypothesis to decision.

